---
description: Keep secrets on the server; never put API keys in the Expo app.
globs: mobile/**,server/**
alwaysApply: true
---

# Secrets stay on the server

- Put keys in `.env` (git-ignored). Never hardcode Grok, Mapbox, Nessie, or Supabase keys.
- The phone app talks to `/api` through `mobile/src/api.js`. Base URL is `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL` only.
- Read helpers in `api.js` return `null` on network failure so screens can show sample data.
- A failed online mutation must never become a successful local claim. Local territory is only for demo mode when no API URL is configured.
- Nessie uses the server's `NESSIE_API_KEY`, HTTPS without redirect fallback, and private account mappings. Remove legacy phone keys during save migration.
- Supabase turf writes use revision-checked RPCs from `server/supabase/schema.sql`; never replace them with a read followed by a blind upsert.
- Eggs are earned by walking. Never spend Nessie savings on eggs.
